@file 137:
@file 138: ### Sroute  
@file 139: # Explanation : Our VDD and GND pads needs to connect to the power rings - otherwise our power rings would just be floating!
@file 140: #               The connection in these pads are on layer M6 respectively M7. 
@file 141: #               We use the special route to tell the tool to connect the `pad_pins` (i.e., the pin connection of the pads) for the net VDD resp. GND
@file 142: #               We also add -inst [..] to only do this for our VDD pads and GND pads.
@@file 143: route_special -connect pad_pin -nets {VDD} -pad_pin_layer_range {M6 M7} -inst [get_db [get_db insts -if {.base_cell == *VDD_*}] .name ]
